":"6:158"},{"pos":36,"ar":"إِنَّا","en_gloss":"Indeed, we","transliteration":"innā","verse_key":"6:158"},{"pos":37,"ar":"مُنتَظِرُونَ","en_gloss":"(are) those who wait","transliteration":"muntaẓirūna","verse_key":"6:158"},{"pos":38,"ar":"١٥٨","en_gloss":"(158)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"6:158"}]},{"verse_key":"6:159","surah":6,"ayah":159,"ar_uthmani":"إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ فَرَّقُوا۟ دِينَهُمْ وَكَانُوا۟ شِيَعًا لَّسْتَ مِنْهُمْ فِى شَىْءٍ ۚ إِنَّمَآ أَمْرُهُمْ إِلَى ٱللَّهِ ثُمَّ يُنَبِّئُهُم بِمَا كَانُوا۟ يَفْعَلُونَ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"As for those who have divided their religion and broken up into factions, have nothing to do with them [Prophet]. Their case rests with God: in time He will tell them about their deeds.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"إِنَّ","en_gloss":"Indeed","transliteration":"inna","verse_key":"6:159"},{"pos":2,"ar":"ٱلَّذِينَ","en_gloss":"those who","transliteration":"alladhīna","verse_key":"6:159"},{"pos":3,"ar":"فَرَّقُوا۟","en_gloss":"divide","transliteration":"farraqū","verse_key":"6:159"},{"pos":4,"ar":"دِينَهُمْ","en_gloss":"their religion","transliteration":"dīnahum","verse_key":"6:159"},{"pos":5,"ar":"وَكَانُوا۟","en_gloss":"and become","transliteration":"wakānū","verse_key":"6:159"},{"pos":6,"ar":"شِيَعًۭا","en_gloss":"sects","transliteration":"shiyaʿan","verse_key":"6:159"},{"pos":7,"ar":"لَّسْتَ","en_gloss":"you are not","transliteration":"lasta","verse_key":"6:159"},{"pos":8,"ar":"مِنْهُمْ","en_gloss":"with them","transliteration":"min'hum","verse_key":"6:159"},{"pos":9,"ar":"فِى","en_gloss":"in","transliteration":"fī","verse_key":"6:159"},{"pos":10,"ar":"شَىْءٍ ۚ","en_gloss":"anything","transliteration":"shayin","verse_key":"6:159"},{"pos":11,"ar":"إِنَّمَآ","en_gloss":"Only","transliteration":"innamā","verse_key":"6:159"},{"pos":12,"ar":"أَمْرُهُمْ","en_gloss":"their affair","transliteration":"amruhum","verse_key":"6:159"},{"pos":13,"ar":"إِلَى","en_gloss":"(is) with","transliteration":"ilā","verse_key":"6:159"},{"pos":14,"ar":"ٱللَّهِ","en_gloss":"Allah","transliteration":"l-lahi","verse_key":"6:159"},{"pos":15,"ar":"ثُمَّ","en_gloss":"then","transliteration":"thumma","verse_key":"6:159"},{"pos":16,"ar":"يُنَبِّئُهُم","en_gloss":"He will inform them","transliteration":"yunabbi-uhum","verse_key":"6:159"},{"pos":17,"ar":"بِمَا","en_gloss":"of what","transliteration":"bimā","verse_key":"6:159"},{"pos":18,"ar":"كَانُوا۟","en_gloss":"they used to","transliteration":"kānū","verse_key":"6:159"},{"pos":19,"ar":"يَفْعَلُونَ","en_gloss":"do","transliteration":"yafʿalūna","verse_key":"6:159"},{"pos":20,"ar":"١٥٩","en_gloss":"(159)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"6:159"}]},{"verse_key":"6:160","surah":6,"ayah":160,"ar_uthmani":"مَن جَآءَ بِٱلْحَسَنَةِ فَلَهُۥ عَشْرُ أَمْثَالِهَا ۖ وَمَن جَآءَ بِٱلسَّيِّئَةِ فَلَا يُجْزَىٰٓ إِلَّا مِثْلَهَا وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُونَ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"Whoever has done a good deed will have it ten times to his credit, but whoever has done a bad deed will be repaid only with its equivalent- they will not be wronged.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"مَن","en_gloss":"Whoever","transliteration":"man","verse_key":"6:160"},{"pos":2,"ar":"جَآءَ","en_gloss":"came","transliteration":"jāa","verse_key":"6:160"},{"pos":3,"ar":"بِٱلْحَسَنَةِ","en_gloss":"with a good deed","transliteration":"bil-ḥasanati","verse_key":"6:160"},{"pos":4,"ar":"فَلَهُۥ","en_gloss":"then for him","transliteration":"falahu","verse_key":"6:160"},{"pos":5,"ar":"عَشْرُ","en_gloss":"(is) ten (times)","transliteration":"ʿashru","verse_key":"6:160"},{"pos":6,"ar":"أَمْثَالِهَا ۖ","en_gloss":"the like of it","transliteration":"amthālihā","verse_key":"6:160"},{"pos":7,"ar":"وَمَن","en_gloss":"And whoever","transliteration":"waman","verse_key":"6:160"},{"pos":8,"ar":"جَآءَ","en_gloss":"came","transliteration":"jāa","verse_key":"6:160"},{"pos":9,"ar":"بِٱلسَّيِّئَةِ","en_gloss":"with an evil deed","transliteration":"bil-sayi-ati","verse_key":"6:160"},{"pos":10,"ar":"فَلَا","en_gloss":"then not","trans